# 📚 FSc Pre-Medical KP Textbook Library

A Streamlit app to read and download Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (KP) Textbook Board
books for **FSc Pre-Medical**:

| Year     | Subjects                                 |
|----------|------------------------------------------|
| 1st Year | Biology, Physics, Chemistry, English     |
| 2nd Year | Biology, Physics, Chemistry, English     |

## Project structure

```
fsc-kp-books/
├── app.py              # main Streamlit app
├── books.json          # catalog of all 8 books
├── requirements.txt    # dependencies
├── books/              # put your PDF files here (create this folder)
├── .streamlit/
│   └── config.toml     # theme
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
```

## Run locally

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
streamlit run app.py
```

## Adding books

You can add each book in **either** of two ways (or both):

### Option A: PDF in the repo
1. Create a folder named `books/`.
2. Save PDFs with these exact names (or edit `books.json`):
   - `1st_year_biology.pdf`, `1st_year_physics.pdf`, `1st_year_chemistry.pdf`, `1st_year_english.pdf`
   - `2nd_year_biology.pdf`, `2nd_year_physics.pdf`, `2nd_year_chemistry.pdf`, `2nd_year_english.pdf`

> GitHub rejects files over 100 MB, and PDFs over ~15 MB won't preview inside
> the app (download still works). For big books use Option B.

### Option B: Google Drive link (recommended for large files)
1. Upload the PDF to Google Drive.
2. Share → **Anyone with the link** → Viewer.
3. Paste the link into the `"link"` field of that book in `books.json`.

## Deploy with GitHub + Streamlit Community Cloud

1. Create a new repository on GitHub (e.g. `fsc-kp-books`).
2. Upload all files in this folder (including `books/` if used):
   ```bash
   git init
   git add .
   git commit -m "Initial commit"
   git branch -M main
   git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/fsc-kp-books.git
   git push -u origin main
   ```
3. Go to [share.streamlit.io](https://share.streamlit.io) and sign in with GitHub.
4. Click **Create app** → choose your repo, branch `main`, main file `app.py`.
5. Click **Deploy**. Every `git push` updates the app automatically.

## Copyright note

Use only official or authorised copies of the KP Textbook Board books. Do not
publish books you do not have the right to distribute. If the repo is public,
anyone can download the PDFs inside it, so consider a private repo or Drive links.

